Two bugs in location-ui's built-in dialogs (the privacy disclaimer, the
"enable positioning" dialog and the others liblocation asks for):

- They started with the response 0, which is "accepted", where -1 is "no
  answer" (as after a close): a liblocation client that asked for the
  disclaimer while the dialog was open got InUse with response 0 and took
  it as accepted.
- The answer to "close" carries the dialog's response, but
  dbus_message_append_args() was given the INT32's value instead of its
  address. With the response 0 (the disclaimer accepted, a dialog's OK)
  libdbus got a NULL pointer and aborted location-ui ("assertion value !=
  NULL failed", signal 6) whenever liblocation closed the dialog after its
  answer; any other response was read as an address.

FreeBSD's Hildon build uses this patch as well
(freebsd/hildon/patches/location-ui/0001 is a link to it).

diff --git a/src/main.c b/src/main.c
index a713607..acb4f34 100644
--- a/src/main.c
+++ b/src/main.c
@@ -107,17 +107,17 @@ static struct client_request_table clireq_table[5] = {
 
 static struct location_ui_dialog funcmap[6] = {
 	{"/com/nokia/location/ui/bt_disconnected",
-	 create_bt_disconnected_dialog, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0},
+	 create_bt_disconnected_dialog, NULL, 0, 0, 0, -1, 0},
 	{"/com/nokia/location/ui/disclaimer",
-	 create_disclaimer_dialog, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0},
+	 create_disclaimer_dialog, NULL, 0, 0, 0, -1, 0},
 	{"/com/nokia/location/ui/enable_gps",
-	 create_enable_gps_dialog, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0},
+	 create_enable_gps_dialog, NULL, 0, 0, 0, -1, 0},
 	{"/com/nokia/location/ui/enable_network",
-	 create_enable_network_dialog, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0},
+	 create_enable_network_dialog, NULL, 0, 0, 0, -1, 0},
 	{"/com/nokia/location/ui/enable_positioning",
-	 create_positioning_dialog, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0},
+	 create_positioning_dialog, NULL, 0, 0, 0, -1, 0},
 	{"/com/nokia/location/ui/enable_agnss",
-	 create_agnss_dialog, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0},
+	 create_agnss_dialog, NULL, 0, 0, 0, -1, 0},
 };
 
 static display_close_map dc_map[2] = {
@@ -580,7 +580,7 @@ DBusMessage *location_ui_close_dialog(location_ui_t * location_ui, GList * list,
 
 	new_msg = dbus_message_new_method_return(msg);
 	dbus_message_append_args(new_msg, DBUS_TYPE_INT32,
-				 dialog->dialog_response_code,
+				 &dialog->dialog_response_code,
 				 DBUS_TYPE_INVALID);
 
 	/* TODO: Review */
